Technically, iX allows arbitrary labels for points -- in fact all objects including regression lines etc. (see the lm example). The intent was to provide the same extended queries we have in our other interactive graphics software -- but the issue is that there is no "natural" interface for selecting covariates of interest - in Klimt, Mondrian etc. you would simply select the variables in the dataset window, but there is no such thing in iPlots as all variables are implicit. So what's missing is the specification of which covariates you want to see. I was hoping to have a look at the before I respond, but this have evolved in the meantime :)

